const thirdNotes=[["Eye Embryology and Development","The eye develops from coordinated contributions of neuroectoderm, surface ectoderm, neural crest and mesoderm. The optic vesicle grows from the forebrain and contacts surface ectoderm, inducing the lens placode, which forms the lens vesicle. The optic cup forms the neural retina and retinal pigment epithelium. The optic stalk becomes the optic nerve. Developmental disturbance may cause congenital anomalies such as coloboma, congenital cataract or microphthalmos.","आँखाको विकासमा neuroectoderm, surface ectoderm, neural crest र mesoderm को संयुक्त योगदान हुन्छ। Forebrain बाट optic vesicle निस्केर surface ectoderm लाई प्रभाव पार्छ र lens placode/lens vesicle बन्छ। Optic cup बाट neural retina र retinal pigment epithelium बन्छ; optic stalk बाट optic nerve विकसित हुन्छ। विकासमा समस्या भए coloboma, congenital cataract वा microphthalmos हुन सक्छ।","Embryology helps explain congenital ocular abnormalities; abnormal red reflex or suspected congenital cataract needs urgent specialist assessment."],["Orbit: Bones, Contents and Functions","The bony orbit is a pyramidal cavity that protects and supports the globe and its associated structures. Its walls are formed by seven bones: frontal, sphenoid, zygomatic, maxilla, palatine, lacrimal and ethmoid. Contents include the eyeball, extraocular muscles, optic nerve, vessels, nerves, lacrimal gland, orbital fat and connective tissue. The optic canal transmits the optic nerve and ophthalmic artery; the superior orbital fissure transmits several cranial nerves and veins.","Bony orbit आँखाको globe र वरिपरिका संरचनालाई सुरक्षा र support दिने पिरामिड आकारको cavity हो। यसको भित्तामा frontal, sphenoid, zygomatic, maxilla, palatine, lacrimal र ethmoid गरी सात हड्डी हुन्छन्। यसभित्र eyeball, extraocular muscles, optic nerve, blood vessels, nerves, lacrimal gland र orbital fat हुन्छन्। Optic canal बाट optic nerve र ophthalmic artery जान्छन्।","Orbital trauma may cause fracture, proptosis, restricted eye movement or optic nerve injury; urgent assessment is important when vision is affected."],["Eyelids, Eyelashes and Meibomian Glands","The upper and lower eyelids protect the ocular surface, spread the tear film during blinking and help prevent excessive light entry. The tarsal plates provide structural support. Meibomian glands within the tarsal plates secrete the lipid layer of tears. Zeis glands are associated with eyelashes and are sebaceous; Moll glands are modified sweat glands. Orbicularis oculi closes the eyelids, while levator palpebrae superioris elevates the upper lid.","माथिल्लो र तल्लो eyelid ले आँखाको सतह जोगाउँछन्, blink गर्दा tear film फैलाउँछन् र धेरै प्रकाश प्रवेश हुनबाट रोक्न सहयोग गर्छन्। Tarsal plate ले आकार र support दिन्छ। यसभित्रका Meibomian gland ले आँसुको lipid layer बनाउँछन्। Zeis gland sebaceous र Moll gland modified sweat gland हुन्। Orbicularis oculi ले eyelid बन्द गर्छ र levator palpebrae superioris ले माथिल्लो eyelid उठाउँछ।","Meibomian gland dysfunction can contribute to evaporative dry eye; lid hygiene and clinical evaluation may be indicated."],["Conjunctiva and Tear Film","The conjunctiva is a thin mucous membrane lining the inner eyelids (palpebral conjunctiva) and covering the anterior sclera (bulbar conjunctiva), stopping at the corneal limbus. It contains goblet cells that produce mucin. The tear film is commonly described as lipid, aqueous and mucin components; it lubricates, nourishes and protects the ocular surface. The lacrimal gland contributes the aqueous component, while meibomian glands provide lipids.","Conjunctiva पातलो mucous membrane हो जसले eyelid को भित्री भाग (palpebral conjunctiva) र अगाडिको sclera (bulbar conjunctiva) ढाक्छ, limbus मा रोकिन्छ। यसका goblet cell ले mucin बनाउँछन्। Tear film मा lipid, aqueous र mucin भाग हुन्छन्; यसले आँखाको सतहलाई चिल्लो, पोषित र सुरक्षित राख्छ। Lacrimal gland ले aqueous र Meibomian gland ले lipid भाग दिन्छ।","Redness, discharge, follicles or papillae may indicate conjunctival disease; assess symptoms and infection-control needs."],["Cornea: Layers, Transparency and Nutrition","The cornea is the transparent, avascular anterior part of the fibrous coat. The classical five layers are epithelium, Bowman's layer, stroma, Descemet's membrane and endothelium. The stroma forms most of corneal thickness. Regular collagen arrangement, controlled hydration and absence of blood vessels support transparency. Nutrition comes mainly from tears, aqueous humour and peripheral vessels. Corneal nerves are highly sensitive and arise from the ophthalmic division of the trigeminal nerve.","Cornea आँखाको बाहिरी fibrous coat को पारदर्शी, रक्तनली नभएको अगाडिको भाग हो। परम्परागत रूपमा यसका पाँच तह epithelium, Bowman's layer, stroma, Descemet's membrane र endothelium हुन्। Stroma ले धेरै मोटाइ बनाउँछ। Collagen को नियमित बनावट, नियन्त्रित hydration र रक्तनली नहुनुले पारदर्शिता कायम गर्छ। पोषण आँसु, aqueous humour र किनाराका रक्तनलीबाट आउँछ। Cornea अत्यन्त संवेदनशील हुन्छ र trigeminal nerve को ophthalmic division बाट sensation पाउँछ।","Corneal abrasion, ulcer or oedema can reduce transparency and threaten vision; contact lens-related pain/redness requires prompt evaluation."],["Sclera and Limbus","The sclera is the tough, opaque white outer coat that protects the globe and provides attachment for extraocular muscles. It is composed mainly of dense collagenous connective tissue. The limbus is the junction between cornea and sclera and contains important structures including the trabecular meshwork region and corneal epithelial stem-cell niche. Episclera lies superficial to sclera and contains vessels.","Sclera आँखाको कडा, अपारदर्शी सेतो बाहिरी तह हो। यसले globe को सुरक्षा गर्छ र extraocular muscles जोडिने स्थान दिन्छ। यो मुख्यतः बाक्लो collagen connective tissue बाट बनेको हुन्छ। Limbus cornea र sclera भेटिने भाग हो; यहाँ trabecular meshwork क्षेत्र र corneal epithelial stem-cell niche हुन्छ। Episclera sclera को बाहिरी सतहमा हुन्छ।","Scleral inflammation may cause deep pain and redness; limbal injury can affect corneal surface healing."],["Uveal Tract: Iris, Ciliary Body and Choroid","The uvea is the vascular middle coat of the eye and consists of iris, ciliary body and choroid. The iris controls pupil diameter through sphincter and dilator muscles. The ciliary body produces aqueous humour and contains the ciliary muscle, which changes zonular tension during accommodation. The choroid is rich in vessels and supplies the outer retina. Inflammation of the uvea is called uveitis.","Uvea आँखाको बीचको रक्तनलीयुक्त तह हो र iris, ciliary body तथा choroid मिलेर बनेको हुन्छ। Iris का sphincter र dilator muscle ले pupil को आकार नियन्त्रण गर्छन्। Ciliary body ले aqueous humour उत्पादन गर्छ र यसको ciliary muscle ले accommodation का बेला zonule को तनाव परिवर्तन गर्छ। Choroid मा धेरै रक्तनली हुन्छन् र यसले बाहिरी retina लाई पोषण दिन्छ। Uvea को inflammation लाई uveitis भनिन्छ।","Pain, photophobia, redness and blurred vision may occur in anterior uveitis and need prompt ophthalmic review."],["Lens, Zonules and Accommodation","The crystalline lens is a transparent, biconvex, avascular structure behind the iris. It is enclosed by a capsule and suspended by zonular fibres attached to the ciliary body. For near focus, ciliary muscle contraction reduces zonular tension and the lens becomes more convex; for distance focus, ciliary muscle relaxes, zonular tension increases and the lens flattens. Age-related loss of lens flexibility contributes to presbyopia.","Crystalline lens iris पछाडि रहेको पारदर्शी, दुवैतर्फ convex र रक्तनली नभएको संरचना हो। यो capsule भित्र हुन्छ र ciliary body सँग zonular fibre ले जोडिएको हुन्छ। नजिक हेर्दा ciliary muscle खुम्चिन्छ, zonule को तनाव घट्छ र lens बढी convex हुन्छ। टाढा हेर्दा ciliary muscle आराम गर्छ, zonular tension बढ्छ र lens च्याप्टो हुन्छ। उमेरसँग lens को लचकता घट्दा presbyopia हुन्छ।","Cataract is loss of lens transparency; sudden visual change or lens displacement needs specialist assessment."],["Vitreous Body and Retinal Support","The vitreous is a transparent gel filling the space between the lens and retina. It is composed mostly of water with collagen and hyaluronic acid. It helps maintain globe shape and allows light transmission. The vitreous is attached more firmly at the vitreous base and at several other sites. Age-related vitreous liquefaction and posterior vitreous detachment may cause floaters and flashes; a sudden shower of floaters, flashes or a curtain-like shadow is an urgent warning sign.","Vitreous lens र retina बीचको खाली भाग भर्ने पारदर्शी gel हो। यसमा धेरै पानीसँग collagen र hyaluronic acid हुन्छ। यसले globe को आकार कायम राख्न र प्रकाश पार हुन सहयोग गर्छ। Vitreous base लगायत केही स्थानमा यसको attachment बलियो हुन्छ। उमेरसँग vitreous पातलो/तरल हुन र posterior vitreous detachment हुन सक्छ, जसले floaters र flashes दिन सक्छ। अचानक धेरै floaters, flashes वा पर्दा झरेजस्तो देखिनु आकस्मिक चेतावनी संकेत हो।","New flashes, sudden floaters or a curtain over vision may indicate retinal tear/detachment and require same-day urgent assessment."],["Retina, Macula and Optic Disc","The retina is the light-sensitive neural layer lining the inner posterior eye. Rods are highly sensitive in dim light and support peripheral vision; cones mediate colour and detailed vision, concentrated in the macula. The fovea, at the centre of the macula, provides the sharpest central vision. The optic disc is where ganglion-cell axons leave the eye to form the optic nerve; it has no photoreceptors and creates the physiological blind spot.","Retina आँखाको पछाडिको भित्री भागमा रहेको प्रकाश संवेदनशील neural तह हो। Rod ले कम प्रकाशमा देख्न र peripheral vision मा सहयोग गर्छ; cone ले रंग र स्पष्ट दृष्टि दिन्छ र macula मा बढी हुन्छ। Macula को बीचको fovea ले सबैभन्दा स्पष्ट central vision दिन्छ। Optic disc बाट ganglion cell का axon बाहिरिएर optic nerve बन्छन्; यहाँ photoreceptor नहुने भएकाले physiological blind spot हुन्छ।","Macular disease affects central vision; optic disc swelling or pallor may signal serious ocular or neurological disease."],["Aqueous Humour, Drainage and Intraocular Pressure","Aqueous humour is produced mainly by the non-pigmented ciliary epithelium of the ciliary processes. It flows from the posterior chamber through the pupil into the anterior chamber and drains mainly through the trabecular meshwork, Schlemm's canal and episcleral veins; a secondary uveoscleral pathway also exists. Intraocular pressure reflects the balance between aqueous production and outflow. Raised IOP is a risk factor for glaucoma but does not alone define the disease.","Aqueous humour मुख्यतः ciliary process को non-pigmented ciliary epithelium ले उत्पादन गर्छ। यो posterior chamber बाट pupil हुँदै anterior chamber मा पुग्छ र मुख्यतः trabecular meshwork, Schlemm's canal तथा episcleral vein बाट बाहिरिन्छ; uveoscleral pathway पनि हुन्छ। Aqueous उत्पादन र निकासको सन्तुलनले intraocular pressure निर्धारण गर्छ। IOP बढ्नु glaucoma को risk factor हो तर यसले मात्र glaucoma पुष्टि गर्दैन।","High IOP may be asymptomatic; acute angle-closure symptoms such as severe pain, red eye, halos, headache and nausea are an emergency."],["Visual Pathway and Pupillary Reflex","Light activates retinal photoreceptors; signals pass through bipolar cells to ganglion cells, whose axons form the optic nerve. At the optic chiasm, fibres from the nasal half of each retina cross, while temporal retinal fibres remain uncrossed. Signals continue through optic tracts to the lateral geniculate nucleus, optic radiations and primary visual cortex. The pupillary light reflex uses the optic nerve as the afferent limb and parasympathetic fibres travelling with the oculomotor nerve as the efferent limb.","प्रकाशले retina का photoreceptor सक्रिय गर्छ; signal bipolar cell हुँदै ganglion cell मा पुग्छ र तिनका axon ले optic nerve बनाउँछन्। Optic chiasm मा प्रत्येक retina को nasal भागका fibre cross हुन्छन्, temporal भागका fibre cross हुँदैनन्। त्यसपछि signal optic tract, lateral geniculate nucleus, optic radiation हुँदै primary visual cortex पुग्छ। Pupillary light reflex मा optic nerve afferent limb र oculomotor nerve सँग जाने parasympathetic fibre efferent limb हुन्छ।","A relative afferent pupillary defect may indicate asymmetric optic nerve or severe retinal dysfunction and needs clinical interpretation."]];
const thirdQ=[["Which embryological structure gives rise to the neural retina?","Neural retina कुन embryological संरचनाबाट विकसित हुन्छ?",["Optic cup","Lens placode","Surface ectoderm alone","Mesoderm"],0,"The optic cup develops into the neural retina and retinal pigment epithelium.","Optic cup बाट neural retina र retinal pigment epithelium विकसित हुन्छ।"],["The optic stalk develops into the:","Optic stalk बाट के विकसित हुन्छ?",["Lens","Optic nerve","Cornea","Iris"],1,"The optic stalk becomes the optic nerve.","Optic stalk बाट optic nerve बन्छ।"],["How many bones form the bony orbit?","Bony orbit बनाउन कति हड्डी सहभागी हुन्छन्?",["Five","Six","Seven","Eight"],2,"The orbit is formed by seven bones.","Orbit सात हड्डीबाट बनेको हुन्छ।"],["Which structure passes through the optic canal?","Optic canal बाट कुन संरचना जान्छ?",["Optic nerve","Facial nerve","Lateral rectus","Nasolacrimal duct"],0,"The optic canal transmits the optic nerve and ophthalmic artery.","Optic canal बाट optic nerve र ophthalmic artery जान्छन्।"],["Meibomian glands mainly contribute which tear-film layer?","Meibomian gland ले आँसुको कुन तह मुख्य रूपमा बनाउँछ?",["Aqueous","Lipid","Mucin","Protein only"],1,"Meibomian glands secrete lipids that reduce tear evaporation.","Meibomian gland ले lipid निकाल्छ जसले आँसु वाष्पीकरण घटाउँछ।"],["The muscle primarily responsible for closing the eyelids is:","Eyelid बन्द गर्ने मुख्य muscle कुन हो?",["Levator palpebrae superioris","Orbicularis oculi","Superior rectus","Müller muscle"],1,"Orbicularis oculi closes the eyelids.","Orbicularis oculi ले eyelid बन्द गर्छ।"],["Conjunctival goblet cells secrete:","Conjunctival goblet cell ले के निकाल्छ?",["Mucin","Aqueous humour","Sebum","Vitreous"],0,"Goblet cells contribute mucin to the tear film.","Goblet cell ले tear film मा mucin दिन्छ।"],["Which corneal layer forms most of the corneal thickness?","Cornea को धेरै मोटाइ कुन तहले बनाउँछ?",["Epithelium","Bowman's layer","Stroma","Endothelium"],2,"The stroma forms most of the corneal thickness.","Stroma ले cornea को धेरै मोटाइ बनाउँछ।"],["The cornea is normally:","सामान्य cornea कस्तो हुन्छ?",["Highly vascular","Avascular and transparent","Opaque and vascular","Pigmented"],1,"The normal cornea is transparent and avascular.","सामान्य cornea पारदर्शी र रक्तनलीरहित हुन्छ।"],["The junction between cornea and sclera is called:","Cornea र sclera भेटिने भागलाई के भनिन्छ?",["Fovea","Limbus","Ora serrata","Optic disc"],1,"The limbus is the corneoscleral junction.","Limbus cornea र sclera भेटिने भाग हो।"],["Which structures make up the uveal tract?","Uveal tract कुन-कुन संरचनाबाट बनेको हुन्छ?",["Cornea, sclera, retina","Iris, ciliary body, choroid","Lens, vitreous, retina","Conjunctiva, cornea, sclera"],1,"The uvea consists of iris, ciliary body and choroid.","Uvea मा iris, ciliary body र choroid पर्छन्।"],["Aqueous humour is produced mainly by the:","Aqueous humour मुख्यतः कहाँ उत्पादन हुन्छ?",["Retinal pigment epithelium","Ciliary processes","Lens capsule","Corneal endothelium"],1,"The ciliary processes produce aqueous humour.","Ciliary process ले aqueous humour उत्पादन गर्छ।"],["Aqueous humour normally flows from posterior to anterior chamber through the:","Aqueous humour posterior बाट anterior chamber मा कुन बाटो जान्छ?",["Optic disc","Pupil","Vitreous base","Scleral spur"],1,"Aqueous passes through the pupil from posterior to anterior chamber.","Aqueous pupil हुँदै posterior बाट anterior chamber मा जान्छ।"],["The main conventional aqueous outflow pathway includes the:","Aqueous निकासको मुख्य conventional pathway मा के पर्छ?",["Trabecular meshwork and Schlemm's canal","Optic nerve and chiasm","Retinal vessels","Lens zonules"],0,"The trabecular meshwork drains aqueous into Schlemm's canal and episcleral veins.","Trabecular meshwork बाट aqueous Schlemm's canal र episcleral vein तर्फ जान्छ।"],["Which part of the retina provides the sharpest central vision?","Retina को कुन भागले सबैभन्दा स्पष्ट central vision दिन्छ?",["Optic disc","Fovea","Ora serrata","Peripheral retina"],1,"The fovea has the highest concentration of cones and provides sharp central vision.","Fovea मा cone धेरै हुन्छन् र स्पष्ट central vision दिन्छ।"],["Rods are primarily responsible for:","Rod photoreceptor मुख्यतः केका लागि जिम्मेवार हुन्छ?",["Colour vision in bright light","Dim-light vision","Accommodation","Pupil constriction"],1,"Rods are highly sensitive in dim illumination and support scotopic vision.","Rod कम प्रकाशमा संवेदनशील हुन्छ र dim-light vision दिन्छ।"],["The optic disc creates a physiological blind spot because it:","Optic disc ले physiological blind spot किन बनाउँछ?",["Contains only cones","Has no photoreceptors","Contains the fovea","Is transparent"],1,"The optic disc is the exit point of ganglion-cell axons and lacks rods and cones.","Optic disc बाट ganglion axon बाहिरिन्छन् र यहाँ rod/cone हुँदैनन्।"],["Which cranial nerve is the afferent limb of the pupillary light reflex?","Pupillary light reflex को afferent limb कुन cranial nerve हो?",["Oculomotor (III)","Optic (II)","Trochlear (IV)","Facial (VII)"],1,"The optic nerve carries the sensory input for the pupillary light reflex.","Optic nerve ले pupillary light reflex को sensory input लैजान्छ।"],["Which cranial nerve carries the parasympathetic efferent pathway for pupil constriction?","Pupil constriction को parasympathetic efferent pathway कुन cranial nerve सँग जान्छ?",["Optic (II)","Trigeminal (V)","Oculomotor (III)","Abducens (VI)"],2,"Parasympathetic fibres travel with the oculomotor nerve to the ciliary ganglion and sphincter pupillae.","Parasympathetic fibre oculomotor nerve हुँदै ciliary ganglion र sphincter pupillae सम्म जान्छ।"],["A sudden curtain-like shadow with flashes and floaters suggests possible:","अचानक पर्दा झरेजस्तो छाया, flashes र floaters देखिएमा के शंका गर्नुपर्छ?",["Simple conjunctivitis","Retinal tear or detachment","Presbyopia","Blepharitis"],1,"These are warning symptoms of retinal tear or detachment and need urgent assessment.","यी retinal tear वा detachment का चेतावनी संकेत हुन् र तुरुन्त परीक्षण चाहिन्छ।"]];
